WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.264 --> 00:00:02.802
-Our first guest tonight is
an Emmy Award-winning actress

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.370
who you know from "Ratched,"

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.138
the "American Horror Story"
franchise,

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:07.607
and "The People vs.
O.J. Simpson."

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:11.143
She is both executive producing
and starring as Linda Tripp

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.345
in "Impeachment:
American Crime Story,"

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:14.948
which airs Tuesdays on FX.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.282
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.051
-Can you at least tell me
did something happen?

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.654
-I told you
I have to talk to Kathleen.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.689
-But will you call me
after you do?

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.091
Here's my card.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:28.193
You can reach me --
-I know how to reach you.

00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:32.531
-Okay. Alright.

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:36.702
-There's a bigger story.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.838
Much bigger than this.

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:42.275
You're barking up
the wrong tree.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.747
-Please welcome back
to the show and studio

00:00:48.747 --> 00:00:50.350
Sarah Paulson, everybody.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.185
♪♪
[ Light applause ]

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:56.756
-[ Laughing ] I like
the world's tiniest applause.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.858
-No, it's not tiny.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.360
-It's like clappity-clap-clap.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.495
-No, they're good.
-Clap, clap, clap.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.263
-They have big,
strong crew hands.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.965
-Clap, clap. I like it.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.067
So we don't have to pretend
there is an audience, right?

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.069
We can call it like it is.
-You can call it like it is.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.205
-Or do people at home think
there's an audience?

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.206
-Well, that's the thing, is
sometimes people will be like,

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:15.808
"God, it was really quiet
last night."

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.510
I'm like,
"No, there's no one here."

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.479
-"She is tanking."

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.046
Unsuccessful.
-So that's good.

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:22.348
I think that's very good.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.716
Especially as you're
the first guest of the night.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.385
It's sort of incumbent on you
to establish

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.587
there's not an audience.
-Great, no pressure of any kind.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.656
Great. Fantastic.
-It's so lovely to see you.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.690
-It's lovely to see you
sans jacket.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.862
-Sans jacket, and you sans
your Linda Tripp outfit.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:39.399
That is a real transfor--
Though I guess your life

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.134
with Ryan Murphy
has been just, like,

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.302
transformation
after transformation.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:46.105
-Yeah, I sort of feel like where
do you go after having two heads

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.975
and playing a heroin addict with
an electrocuted head of hair,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:52.011
Chia Pet thing,
Chia Pet Marcia Clark wig.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.246
I think Linda Tripp feels like
a natural progression to me.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:55.881
I don't really know
where you go.

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:57.984
-There must be a fair amount of
discussion, though,

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.752
as far as, like,
how do you even go about

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.988
the costuming
for something like that.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.790
The great thing about it,
I will say, is, like,

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.259
when it starts and you're
watching it, you're like,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.328
"That's Sarah?" And then you
forget that's Sarah,

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.830
which is, I guess, the whole
point of, like, doing acting,

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.233
is making you forget
who the actual actor is.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.936
-Yeah, I think a lot of times
people only want to play things

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.605
that are close to home, but I'm
like, "I want to be a pirate."

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.340
I want a peg leg
and a black tooth.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.674
If I'm not having that,
then I'm not really --

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:24.310
-I guess a Ryan Murphy role
really takes care of --

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.611
Wait, is there your new --

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:26.813
Hold on. I want to make sure
I get the photo right.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.081
This is your newest, right?

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.683
-This is Tuberculosis Karen.
-Tuberculosis Karen.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:34.654
-Now, when Ryan calls and goes,
"I've got a great part for you,"

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.456
I mean, he knows you're gonna
jump at the chance to play --

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.157
-He does, because I'm a glutton
for punishment.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.191
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:40.226
-And let me just say.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.861
I mean, this is no makeup,
right?

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.330
-This is me on your average
Monday morning, guys.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.967
[ Laughter ]
This is sort of how I wake up.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:51.237
Good morning, everybody!
Morning!

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.539
-I got to give the set
photographer credit

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.507
because they really grabbed
a perfect expression

00:02:55.507 --> 00:02:57.109
for Tuberculosis Karen.
-They sure did.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.411
Look at my sad eyebrows.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:01.247
So, see, as Linda,
I had to erase them

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.082
because her eyebrows are
different than mine.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.284
-Right.
-And so one of the ways

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.051
we figured out how we could
transform my face

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.320
was to bleach them.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.055
But when you bleach them
and shave them,

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.424
you have to walk around
without them all of the time.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.792
-Yeah.
-All of the time.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.794
Not drunk at all, totally sober.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.063
And so Ryan came up with
the idea to sort of do this

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.165
Warholian -- Warhalian?

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.332
-No, Warholian.
-Warholian.

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:21.534
-Warholian.
-Warholian.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.635
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.937
-Eyebrow above
the painted-out bleach.

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:28.107
And so it was
all a solve to hide Linda.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.042
-For people who are watching
when this airs,

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.945
Tuberculosis Karen actually
has two sets of eyebrows.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.346
-She has two sets of eyebrows --

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.947
the bleached ones
and then the bigger eyebrow.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.250
-So everybody sees her and they
think things aren't going well

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.717
for Tuberculosis Karen.
Joke's on you.

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:40.486
She's got two sets. Things
are going so well for her.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.987
-Yeah, exactly.
-She's got doubles.

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:44.557
-She's got doubles.
-You have a dog, Winnie.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.924
-I do have a dog, Winnie,
that I got

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.259
in the beginning
of the pandemic.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.394
-People know about Winnie.
-People know about Winnie.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.662
-You have shared Winnie
with the world.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.731
-Winnie has been shared.
-We're going to break some news.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.566
-Let's break the Internet.
-You got a second dog.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.702
-Kim Kardashian
got nothing on us.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.637
Okay, come on.
-You got a second dog.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.739
-I got a second dog.
-What's the new dog's name?

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.741
-Her name is Louise,
but I call her Weezy.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.009
-Weezy. Great. As you should.

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:06.011
So you got Weezy and Winnie.
-Weezy and Winnie.

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:07.079
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.647
-And how are they doing?

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:11.217
-It seemed okay
in the beginning,

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.952
but then there have been
a couple of tense moments

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.221
where they were -- let's just
say teeth I didn't know

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.156
my dog had were on display.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:20.059
-So this is a photo of them
and I guess

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.161
someone made the argument
that they're playing.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.929
-Sure.
-But this is...

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.732
One of these dogs does not look
like they're having fun.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.101
Look at that.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.468
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.003
-But also, hello.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.339
She looks like she's flying.
-Yeah.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.874
-But this one also,
the dog is like, "Duh!"

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.075
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.711
And Winnie is like,
"I said back, my lady!"

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.212
I just love it.
-It's true.

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:42.581
It is like this one is like, "I
think the date is going good."

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.417
-"I think she really likes me."
-"Yeah, I think it's good."

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.886
-"She really likes me."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.455
-So are they, in general,
would you say it's working?

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.524
-I think it's happening. The
very thing that I wanted to do

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.994
was to prevent my dog from --
I anthropomorphize the dog,

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:57.963
so if she looks out the window,
I think she's looking longingly

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:00.566
for her Prince or Princess
Charming and it's not coming.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.502
So I brought the dog home
to try to --

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:05.604
And then as you can see,
it's going swimmingly.

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.540
-Something else that's going --
I want to give you a shout-out

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.941
because you were mentioned
last week on the show.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.843
Amanda Peet has a wonderful show
called "The Chair."

00:05:11.843 --> 00:05:13.545
And she basically
gave you credit

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:14.847
for being casting director.
-Yes.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.283
-You connected her with
Sandra Oh, who's a friend.

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:19.485
You probably had the number
in your phone.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.453
-Yes, e-mail.
-But then Holland Taylor,

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:22.688
who was a lot easier
for you to contact.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:23.956
-Yeah, I just basically
went in the other room

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.959
and said, "Hey, Dumb-Dumb,
please do the show

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.194
and don't be crazy
and also don't make me look bad

00:05:29.194 --> 00:05:30.563
to my best friend."

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.564
-Not that I think
Holland could ever make you

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.600
look bad as an actor.
-Never.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.002
-But in social situations,

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.304
I'm sure she embarrasses you
all the time.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.239
-She's embarrassing me
constantly!

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.807
-But as an actor, not once.
-Never.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.342
-But she's so good in it.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:45.177
-She's so good in it.
-Yeah.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.347
-Funny. I mean, but, you know,

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.481
Holland is that funny
all the time.

00:05:49.481 --> 00:05:52.418
I took a video of her in
the hotel room the other night.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.488
Not creepy. It's not a creepy
video, guys, super not creepy.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:58.824
But of her singing a song called
"It's Choco Coffee Time"

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:00.726
set to like "Howdy Doody Time"

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:02.328
because she drinks a cup of
coffee in the morning

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:06.199
that is a vat of hot chocolate
and international coffee creamer

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.267
and then, like,
a tiny drop of espresso,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.270
and she needs her -- so she's
like, ♪ It's choco coffee time ♪

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.471
♪ It's choco ♪

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:14.040
And she started doing a dance,
and I just --

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.476
I recorded it,
and if you are really lucky,

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:18.110
you'd get that video
before I leave.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.980
-Well, I certainly hope one day
I'll get it.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.948
-She's gonna kill me
for telling that story

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:24.883
because she was spinning around
in her little pajamas.

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:26.619
♪ Choco coffee ♪
-Well, when you drink that much

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:28.420
hot chocolate,
you're gonna spin around.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.223
It's got to go somewhere.
-It was really something.

